# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signing material and Apple credentials — NEVER commit these.
#
# The .p8 is the catastrophic one: it signs developer tokens for your team and
# does not expire, so anyone who gets it can mint tokens as you until the key is
# revoked. The rest are less severe but still leak your team identity, and none
# of them belong in a repository.
#
# Note the helper does NOT need a provisioning profile — MusicKit validates the
# app's Team ID and bundle id server-side (see docs/PERMISSIONS.md), so there is
# no reason for one to be here at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.p8
AuthKey_*.p8
*.cer
*.p12
*.pfx
*.certSigningRequest
*.provisionprofile
*.mobileprovision
*.keychain
*.keychain-db
embedded.provisionprofile

# Private keys of any flavour. certifi ships a CA bundle as .pem, but that lives
# in .venv/ and dist/, both ignored above.
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# Built Swift helper: a signed binary, rebuilt by swift/amcp-musickit/build.sh.
swift/amcp-musickit/AMCPMusicKit.app/
swift/**/*.app/

# Local runtime state that can contain tokens or library data.
*.token.json
music_user_token.json
developer_token.json
harvested_token.json
